Short:        VLC media player, unofficial OS3 port
Uploader:     (Dale fills this in at upload time)
Author:       VideoLAN (VLC); Amiga port: Dale Kirkwood
Type:         gfx/show
Version:      0.1
Requires:     OpenRTG, OpenGPU, OpenMedia, AHI; OpenSocket for streams
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

An unofficial port of the VLC media player to AmigaOS 3.x, not made or
endorsed by VideoLAN.

Video goes through OpenRTG and OpenGPU (a window or full screen on any
monitor, frames scaled and converted without a copy through the CPU), decoding
through OpenMedia (the graphics chip's video engines, the PC's on AmigaChrome,
a PiStorm's VideoCore, or FFmpeg on the CPU), sound through AHI and network
streams through OpenSocket, with a GadTools window.

Status: planned; this readme is ready for the first release.

Licences: libVLC, libvlccore and most modules are LGPL 2.1 or later, as are
the Amiga modules (Copyright (c) 2026 Dalsin Limited); the player and some
modules are GPL 2 or later; FFmpeg keeps its own. The full texts and the
source come with the archive. VLC and the cone are trademarks of VideoLAN.

Source: https://github.com/DalsinAI/openamigavlc (the Amiga port) and
https://code.videolan.org/videolan/vlc (VLC)
